<VI _name="lvbd_graft_paste.vi" description="First half of lvai_graft_diagram. Copies the WHOLE block diagram of Source VI (a generated scaffold) and pastes it into Target VI (a copy of a supplied VI whose front panel must survive), through TopLevelDiagram Select All, Copy Selection and Paste, then saves Target in place.\0A\0ABOTH VIs ARE OPENED IN THE IDE's OWN APPLICATION INSTANCE, reached through Application\3AProject\3AActive Project, so a project must be open and active. Copy Selection and Paste go through the SYSTEM CLIPBOARD, so whatever was on it is replaced.\0A\0AA PASTED TERMINAL BECOMES A NEW CONTROL. LabVIEW gives every pasted control a label that is unique on the target panel, so a control the supplied panel already carries arrives as a duplicate with a numeric suffix - Start 2 - and the duplicates carry all the wires. Labels Before and Labels After are returned so the caller can tell the duplicates from the originals by label alone; the second half of the graft swaps them.\0A\0AMeasured 2026-09-30 on a CLD exam template\3A 14 controls after the paste, the 7 supplied ones and 7 duplicates, error 0, 204 ms.">
